\section{Summary and Further Reading}\label{sec:summary-50}

Effect systems extend type systems with information about the computational behavior of programs. From simple effect annotations to algebraic effects and handlers, they provide a spectrum of tools for reasoning about purity, resource usage, and side effects. The algebraic effects approach, with its modular composition and flexible handling, represents the state of the art in effect system design.

For further reading, we recommend Plotkin and Power's foundational paper~\cite{plotkin2003}, the Koka language documentation~\cite{leijen2019}, and the survey by Pretnar~\cite{pretnar2015} on algebraic effects and handlers.
